htsStatus":"review-required","geometryStatus":"draft","attribution":"Open Landmarks; contains © OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL-1.0","references":[{"title":"File:Centre Pompidou @ Beaubourg @ Paris (15448205062).jpg","author":"Guilhem Vellut from Annecy, France","license":"CC BY 2.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","sourcePage":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Centre_Pompidou_@_Beaubourg_@_Paris_(15448205062).jpg","sourceSha1":"abd7027763d575779187162bff4aa27bd8f3a39f","use":"visual-reference-only","view":"West plaza facade: exposed white frame, glazed bays and external zigzag escalator. Photograph has temporary banners; those are not modeled."}],"aliases":[],"authors":["Open Landmarks contributors"],"artisticLicense":"CC-BY-4.0","spatialDataLicense":"ODbL-1.0","licenseScope":"CC BY applies to original artistic contributions only; ODbL applies to OSM-derived spatial data. Reference photographs retain their own licenses.","assistance":"AI-assisted architectural interpretation and procedural recipe authoring; deterministic Python/Blender export. No photographic textures.","review":{"status":"pending","reviewer":null,"checks":{}},"modelingNotes":["The OSM outline and 42 m height set the glazed rectangular volume. No building parts are mapped.","The Centre Pompidou architectural guide identifies the white external frame, west-side diagonal escalator and blue air, green water and red circulation services. Members and pipe spacing are schematic map-scale interpretations.","The west escalator is a broad, glazed diagonal circulation tube with red rails and repeated landings. It remains a schematic exterior, not a functioning machine. Blue, green and yellow service runs carry the colour code along the east elevation."],"source":{"url":"/objects/aab46545ec6d9b81080b732bd8a408a213df79901f6221378537c8a988441c5b/source.blend.gz","bytes":135301,"sha256":"aab46545ec6d9b81080b732bd8a408a213df79901f6221378537c8a988441c5b"},"spatialSource":{"url":"